# Love Story — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` (or export these in your shell / hosting dashboard) and change
# what you need. Every value here has a working default for local development,
# so an empty file is a valid file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The backend does NOT load a .env file by itself — there is no dotenv
# dependency and no build step in this project. These are ordinary environment
# variables: export them, or set them in whatever runs the server.
#
#   LOVE_STORY_ENV=development uvicorn backend.main:app --port 8000
#
# Nothing secret belongs in this file. It is committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which world this is: "development" (the default) or "production".
#
# It decides two things and nothing else:
#   · whether the session cookie is sent with Secure (production: yes)
#   · whether the loopback CORS rule applies (development: yes)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOVE_STORY_ENV=development

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the archive lives. Both default to inside the repository, which is what
# local development wants:
#
#   LOVE_STORY_DB_PATH      backend/lovestory.db
#   LOVE_STORY_UPLOAD_DIR   backend/uploads/
#
# On a server, mount one persistent volume and point both at it. The database
# and the photographs must be on the SAME volume: a backup has to contain both,
# and a photograph whose row survives a restore without its file is worse than
# no photograph at all.
#
#   LOVE_STORY_DB_PATH=/data/lovestory.db
#   LOVE_STORY_UPLOAD_DIR=/data/uploads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOVE_STORY_DB_PATH=
LOVE_STORY_UPLOAD_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which front-end origins may call this API, comma separated.
#
# Leave it EMPTY when the API is served from the same site as the front-end —
# the recommended setup, where a reverse proxy sends /api and /uploads here.
# Same-origin requests are always allowed and need no entry.
#
# Set it only when the front-end genuinely lives on another origin:
#
#   LOVE_STORY_FRONTEND_ORIGINS=https://ourstory.example,https://www.ourstory.example
#
# Never "*". A wildcard origin and credentialed requests cannot be combined,
# and this API is not public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOVE_STORY_FRONTEND_ORIGINS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session cookie.
#
#   LOVE_STORY_COOKIE_SECURE    default: off in development, ON in production
#   LOVE_STORY_COOKIE_SAMESITE  default: lax   (one of lax, strict, none)
#
# "lax" is correct whenever the front-end and the API share a site, which
# includes one behind a reverse proxy at /api. "none" is only for a genuinely
# different site, and browsers accept it only together with Secure — so the
# backend quietly keeps "lax" if you ask for "none" without Secure.
#
# Local development over plain http MUST leave Secure off, or the browser will
# never send the cookie back and signing in will appear to do nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOVE_STORY_COOKIE_SECURE=false
LOVE_STORY_COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Private Archive.
#
#   LOVE_STORY_PRIVACY_UNLOCK_MINUTES   default: 10
#
# How long a privacy-password unlock lasts, measured from the last time the
# private archive was actually USED — not from the last time a page asked
# whether it was still open. Ten minutes is the point of the feature: the
# account's sign-in lasts a month, this lasts long enough to read something.
#
# The cookie setting above now matters to the photographs as well. /uploads is
# no longer a public static directory: every photograph is served through a
# route that checks the session, the space membership and (for a private
# memory) the private ACL. A browser sends the session cookie with an <img>
# request when the front-end and the API are on the same SITE — same origin, or
# two subdomains of one domain, or the recommended reverse proxy that serves
# both /api and /uploads from one address. Front-end and API on genuinely
# different sites need SameSite=none with Secure, or the photographs will
# answer 401 and appear broken.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOVE_STORY_PRIVACY_UNLOCK_MINUTES=10
